---
title: add_to_bloom (Osaka bloom.py)
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> q_init
    q_init --> q_hash : hashed = keccak256(bloom_entry)
    q_hash --> q_iter : for idx in (0, 2, 4)
    q_iter --> q_compute_bit : bit_to_set = from_be_bytes(hashed[idx..idx+2]) AND 0x07FF
    q_compute_bit --> q_set_index : bit_index = 0x07FF - int(bit_to_set)
    q_set_index --> q_calc_byte : byte_index = bit_index // 8
    q_calc_byte --> q_calc_value : bit_value = 1 LEFT_SHIFT (7 - (bit_index MOD 8))
    q_calc_value --> q_set_bit : bloom[byte_index] = bloom[byte_index] OR bit_value
    q_set_bit --> q_iter : more indices remaining
    q_set_bit --> q_final : all indices processed
    q_final --> [*]

    note right of q_iter
        INV: idx only takes values from {0, 2, 4}
        (exactly 3 hash functions)
    end note

    note right of q_compute_bit
        INV: bit_to_set is always in range [0, 2047]
        (11-bit mask 0x07FF)
    end note

    note right of q_calc_byte
        INV: byte_index is always in range [0, 255]
    end note

    note right of q_calc_value
        INV: bit_value is always a single-bit
        power of 2 in range [1, 128]
    end note

    note right of q_init
        INV: bloom bytearray is always exactly 256 bytes
    end note
